{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.122.6.a001", "note": "Bare direct object reached through a supplied 'for'; the preposition joins the verb under rule 44. Margin 'Salute ye Jerusalem' set aside.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.122.6.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.122.6.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.122.6.a002", "note": "Supplied 'the' on the construct (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.122.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.122.6.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.122.6.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.122.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.122.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.122.6.a004", "note": "Finite verb keeps auxiliary and lexical verb; its explicit subject is the participle, which takes the English 'They ... that' (rule 17). Margin 'May they' set aside.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.122.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.122.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.122.6.a005", "note": "Anarthrous substantival participle takes the supplied 'They ... that' under rule 46, discontinuous around the verb (rule 25). Alternative: 'They' as the verb's subject pronoun under rule 17; rejected because the participle is the clause's explicit subject and the ASV's 'that' frame realizes it.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.122.6.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.122.6.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.122.6.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.122.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.122.6.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}], "ref": "PSA.122.6", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
